### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop | Dropdown aligned to right |
| Mobile | Full-width dropdown |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | region with aria-label "Notifications" |
| Heading | h3 "Notifications" |
| Keyboard | Arrow keys navigate, Enter to select, Escape to close |
| Focus management | Focus returns to trigger on close |
| Live region | Announces new notifications |

---

## Open Questions / Assumptions

| # | Item | Status | Notes |
|---|------|--------|-------|
| 1 | Progress bar component | Assumption — flagged for DS owner | ProjectCard and CycleCard reference a progress bar (percentage fill + label). This is a common UI pattern but not defined in the current design-system. If the DS owner wants to formalize it, it should be added to the component catalog with its own a11y contract. The wireframe treats it as a resolved element; the DS can adopt or redefine it. |
| 2 | "Updated" transient state on IssueCard/ProjectCard | Resolved — proportional | The real-time "updated" state (subtle flash/highlight) is described behaviorally without a dedicated sketch. This is proportional: the state is a transient visual effect (200–500ms highlight), not a structural layout change. The populated-state sketch + the annotation table's behavior column are sufficient for an engineer to build it. A dedicated sketch would add coverage without buildability value. |
